    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d9-a11">

                <pb facs="0154" n="26" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg26"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 11 in No. 28.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Francis to Baron Pasetti</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-04-18"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 18,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your excellency’s note, No. 9005–7, of the date of April 15,
                    1885, together with an inclosure embracing evidence relative to the case of
                    Harry Rice, arrested at Lippa, in Hungary, in February last, charged with owing
                    military service to the Imperial Royal Government.</p>
                <p>In response to the request contained in the note of your excellency I shall, upon
                    receipt of information from my Government, hasten to communicate to the imperial
                    royal ministry “the results of the events” regarding this affair as instruction
                    may be given me thereon.</p>
                <p>I avail, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN M. FRANCIS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
